  <h1 class="main-title">Zuzuzoo — Privacy Policy</h1>

  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> August 24, 2026</p>
  <p>Operator: <strong>Siarhei Kazachonak</strong> (<a href="mailto:kazachonaksiarhei@gmail.com">kazachonaksiarhei@gmail.com</a>), Poland.</p>
  <p>This Privacy Policy applies to the Android version of Zuzuzoo with Google Play package name <strong>com.ohhimark.zuzuzoo</strong>.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">1. Overview</h2>
  <p>Zuzuzoo (the “App”) is an educational animal-learning app designed for young children ages 1–4 and used under a parent’s or guardian’s supervision. This Policy explains what information the Android App and its service providers process, why it is processed, how long it is retained, and the choices available to parents and guardians.</p>
  <p>We follow data-minimization principles. The App has no advertising, no user account registration, no social features, and no third-party behavioral analytics or remote crash-reporting SDK. We do not sell personal information and do not use information for targeted advertising or cross-app tracking.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">2. Information we do not collect from children</h2>
  <p>The App does not ask a child to provide a name, email address, phone number, postal address, photograph, voice recording, contacts, precise or approximate location, or other information that directly identifies or contacts the child.</p>
  <p>The Android App does not request access to the camera, microphone, contacts, location, phone state, Bluetooth devices, or advertising identifier. It does not intentionally access or transmit the Android Advertising ID (AAID), Android ID, IMEI, IMSI, SIM serial, build serial, Wi-Fi BSSID, MAC address, or SSID.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">3. Information processed by the App</h2>

  <h3 class="subheading">3.1. Local gameplay and settings</h3>
  <p>The App stores gameplay state and preferences locally on the device, such as the selected language, onboarding status, volume-related state, and premium entitlement cache. This information is used only to provide App functionality and is not sent to our own server.</p>
  <p>Depending on the parent’s Android and Google backup settings, Android may back up or transfer some local App preferences through Google’s system backup service. The Operator does not receive or control that backup. A parent can control Android backup in the device’s Google and system settings.</p>

  <h3 class="subheading">3.2. Subscription and purchase information</h3>
  <p>Purchases are initiated by a parent or guardian and processed by Google Play. We do not receive or store complete payment card or bank account details.</p>
  <p>To show subscription products, complete purchases, restore access, prevent purchase fraud, and validate premium entitlement, the App uses Google Play Billing and RevenueCat. The following information may be processed:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google Play purchase history and purchase-related records, such as the product or base-plan identifier, purchase token or transaction reference, purchase date, subscription status, renewal state, and entitlement status.</li>
    <li>A random anonymous RevenueCat App User ID generated by the RevenueCat SDK. The App does not provide RevenueCat with a Zuzuzoo account name, email address, or custom user account ID because the App has no account system.</li>
    <li>Limited technical information needed to operate the subscription service, such as platform, App version, operating-system version, device type, locale, currency, SDK version, and network information such as IP address as processed by the service provider.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This information is required for subscription functionality and purchase validation. RevenueCat also uses purchase history for its subscription dashboard and service analytics. It is not used by us for advertising or profiling children.</p>

  <h3 class="subheading">3.3. Support communications</h3>
  <p>If a parent or guardian voluntarily contacts us by email, we receive the sender’s email address and the contents of the message. For purchase support, a parent may optionally provide a Google Play order number or anonymous purchase details. Please do not send a child’s name, birth date, photograph, voice recording, or other unnecessary personal information.</p>

  <h3 class="subheading">3.4. Legal pages</h3>
  <p>When a parent opens the Privacy Policy or Terms of Service inside the App, the App loads a static HTTPS page hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may process ordinary web-request information, such as IP address, browser or WebView user agent, requested URL, and request time, under GitHub’s own privacy terms. JavaScript, file access, and content access are disabled in the App’s legal-document WebView.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">4. How we use information</h2>
  <p>Information described in this Policy is used only to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide local educational gameplay and remember App preferences.</li>
    <li>Display available subscriptions and localized Google Play pricing.</li>
    <li>Process, verify, restore, and maintain subscription access.</li>
    <li>Prevent purchase fraud and resolve billing or entitlement problems.</li>
    <li>Respond to support, privacy, or legal requests from a parent or guardian.</li>
    <li>Comply with applicable legal, accounting, consumer-protection, and regulatory obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use this information for targeted advertising, behavioral profiling, sale of data, marketing to children, or tracking users across unrelated apps or websites.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">5. Legal bases for processing</h2>
  <p>For users in the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, and other jurisdictions that require a legal basis, processing is based on:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Performance of a contract:</strong> providing paid subscription features, validating purchases, and restoring access requested by the parent or guardian.</li>
    <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> securing the service, preventing purchase fraud, maintaining accurate entitlement records, and responding to support requests, balanced against the limited and anonymous nature of the information.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligations:</strong> retaining or disclosing information where required by tax, accounting, consumer-protection, court, or regulatory rules.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If the App’s practices change in a way that requires verified parental consent, we will obtain that consent before collecting the additional information.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">6. Service providers and disclosure</h2>
  <p>We disclose only the information necessary to the following service providers:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Play / Google Payments:</strong> app distribution, payment processing, purchase records, subscription management, fraud prevention, refunds, and system backup where enabled. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat, Inc.:</strong> subscription product retrieval, purchase validation, anonymous customer records, entitlement status, restoration, and subscription service analytics. <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RevenueCat Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li><strong>GitHub, Inc.:</strong> hosting of the static Privacy Policy and Terms pages that a parent may open. <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>These providers may process information in countries outside Poland or the European Economic Area and apply their own security, retention, and legal-compliance practices. Where required, transfers are protected by recognized legal mechanisms such as adequacy decisions or Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>
  <p>We may also disclose information if required by law, a valid court order, or a competent public authority, or when reasonably necessary to protect users, the App, or our legal rights.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">7. Data Safety disclosure</h2>
  <p>The Google Play Data safety form for the released App must be kept consistent with the App and this Policy. Because RevenueCat processes subscription records, the form should disclose <strong>Financial info — Purchase history</strong> as collected, required for the subscription feature, not processed only ephemerally, and used for App functionality and service analytics. Any future SDK, RevenueCat integration, or data practice must be evaluated and the form updated before release.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">8. Retention and deletion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Local App data:</strong> remains on the device until the App data is cleared or the App is uninstalled. A system backup may restore some preferences if the parent has enabled Android backup.</li>
    <li><strong>RevenueCat subscription data:</strong> is retained while needed to provide, restore, audit, and secure subscription access and as described in RevenueCat’s retention practices. Some purchase records may need to be retained for fraud prevention or legal obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Play purchase data:</strong> is retained by Google under Google’s policies and applicable payment, tax, and accounting requirements.</li>
    <li><strong>Support email:</strong> is retained only as long as reasonably needed to answer the request, maintain a support record, or satisfy a legal obligation, and is then deleted or anonymized.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A parent or guardian may request access, correction, or deletion by emailing <a href="mailto:kazachonaksiarhei@gmail.com">kazachonaksiarhei@gmail.com</a> with the subject “Zuzuzoo Android Privacy Request.” Include only the information needed to locate the subscription, such as an optional Google Play order number. We may ask for limited verification to avoid deleting another customer’s record. We aim to respond within 30 days, subject to applicable law.</p>
  <p>Deleting a RevenueCat customer record does not cancel a Google Play subscription and may not delete records that Google must retain. Subscriptions must be cancelled separately in Google Play. We may retain the minimum information required by law or necessary to establish, exercise, or defend legal claims.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">9. Children’s privacy and parental controls</h2>
  <p>The child-facing experience does not request personal information, display advertising, or contain external web links. Subscription and settings areas are intended for parents and protected by an adult-directed parent gate where applicable.</p>
  <p>Parents and guardians should complete purchases, review legal documents, and manage Google Play or Family Link controls themselves. If we learn that information from a child was provided to us contrary to this Policy, we will delete it unless retention is legally required. Contact us immediately using the address in Section 13.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">10. Security</h2>
  <p>Subscription and legal-page traffic uses HTTPS/TLS. Purchases are processed by Google Play rather than by the App, and the App does not store complete payment credentials. Access to RevenueCat and developer systems is restricted to authorized use.</p>
  <p>No electronic system can be guaranteed completely secure. If you believe information associated with the App has been exposed or misused, contact us at <a href="mailto:kazachonaksiarhei@gmail.com">kazachonaksiarhei@gmail.com</a>.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">11. Privacy rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where the parent or guardian lives, they may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to processing; obtain data portability; and lodge a complaint with a data-protection authority. These rights may be limited where we cannot reasonably identify the anonymous record or where retention is legally required.</p>
  <p>Residents of Poland may contact the President of the Personal Data Protection Office (UODO). Residents elsewhere may contact their local supervisory or consumer-protection authority.</p>

  <h2 class="heading">12. Changes to this Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Policy when the App, service providers, or legal requirements change. We will update the effective date and publish the revised Policy at the same public location. If a change materially affects children’s information or requires parental consent, we will provide additional notice or obtain consent as required before the new practice begins.</p>

